  "legacy_defects": [
    "orgtree_self_relaunch accepts a reason and records none of it: the maintenance request says 'agent requested desktop maintenance' and the org event's detail is {}",
    "orgtree_self_update is not refused as a renamed tool under the desktop-managed profile (it is absent from api._DESKTOP_LEGACY_RESTART_TOOLS) and records a maintenance request with action 'update' and the caller's target (mailhub and both accepted), options the renamed V2 verbs refuse",
    "orgtree_self_update's receipt keeps target, which the desktop-managed result does not carry, so its desktop receipt keeps nothing"
  ],
  "scope": "Legacy boundary of the desktop relaunch entry points and the deprecated orgtree_self_update (P01 relaunch-cards item) on disposable SQLite, per product profile. Under the desktop-managed profile the real desktop maintenance adapter runs and writes the machine-wide request file in the temporary data root; under the non-desktop profile the launch and the quiesce are spies. The doors, the gates, the receipts, save and reload are real. Legacy conformance evidence only: not a runtime census, not PostgreSQL or Rust qualification."
}
